      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(ai): preserve thinking blocks on historical turns with tool calls",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nFixes an issue where users disabling reasoning playback (setting `replayThinkingEnabled` to `false` or reasoning to `off`) would encounter Anthropic API validation errors on subsequent turns of a conversation that contained tool calls. This happened because removing the `thinking` block from historical assistant turns that also contain `tool_use` blocks violates Anthropic's API schema requirements (which mandate that a tool-use block must be accompanied by its preceding thinking block in the assistant turn).\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nModified the thinking block cleanup logic in `packages/ai/src/providers/anthropic.ts` to preserve thinking blocks for any historical assistant turns that contain one or more tool calls, even when `replayThinkingEnabled` is configured to `false`.\n\n## User Impact\n\nPrevents conversation crashes and API validation errors on Anthropic models when reasoning is turned off and the agent makes tool calls.\n\n## Evidence\n\nAdded unit test `preserves thinking blocks in history assistant turns containing tool calls even when replayThinkingEnabled is false` in `packages/ai/src/providers/anthropic.test.ts` (passed all 51 tests).\n\n### Real Behavior Proof\n\nVerified via test execution output:\n```\n ✓ |unit| packages/ai/src/providers/anthropic.test.ts (51 tests) 100ms\n```\nWhen `replayThinkingEnabled` is false, previously all historical assistant turns had their thinking blocks stripped. If those assistant turns also contained tool calls, they were sent to Anthropic with only `tool_use` blocks and no `thinking` block, causing API validation failure. With this fix, we preserve thinking blocks for historical turns that contain one or more tool calls, keeping Anthropic API requests valid.\n",
        "branch": "fix/6.2-anthropic-thinking-tool-rejection",
